{"kind":"assert","text":"Review of draft 3 of the client design note (commit 2ef973ed, answer 07cd213d). This act ratifies nothing.\n\nDraft 3 answers gap A, gap B and each of the seven corrections of 98d6a650, and each answer holds. I found no new gap. I recommend that Hugh ratify draft 3.\n\nGap A. The present values of section 3, rules 1 and 2 of section 6, and the rule for `edit` in section 8 keep each text that the member typed. The sentence on a draft store that differs from the sealed intent also covers an edit in a second tab that passes the first tab's write to custody.\n\nGap B. `absent` and the new row of section 7 close a dead signing, so custody drops the envelope of each earlier signing.\n\nTwo points of wording remain. Neither needs a new draft. Each can go into the request for its build step.\n\n1. The new row of section 7 says \"one time\". A read that fails while the feed is down must not count, or the offline phone of section 14 still keeps each envelope. The rule: at the first journal read after the death that reaches the head, call `absent` if the replica does not hold the key. This point belongs to C3.\n2. Section 8 says that an edit of a taken draft stops with `taken`. In the tab that submitted, the slot of a taken draft is empty, and an edit there starts a new draft. So the stop applies when the tab's published view still shows that draft in the slot. Invariant 1 already forces this reading, because the other reading makes two entries for one intention. This point belongs to C4."}